{"id":"29e21ca5bc688eac1855165f049cd552b0f17d71","axis":"silent","repo":"saltstack/salt","sha":"29e21ca5bc688eac1855165f049cd552b0f17d71","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"changelog/70404.removed.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@","+Removed the deprecated M2Crypto-based X.509 execution and state modules.","+The cryptography-based `x509_v2` modules are now the only implementation","+exposed as `x509`; `features:x509_v2` no longer selects the old modules.","+","+Removed compatibility with legacy arguments. See the","+[migration guide](https://docs.saltproject.io/en/master/ref/modules/all/salt.modules.x509_v2.html#x509-migration-3009)","+for the required changes and new defaults."],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"salt/client/ssh/wrapper/x509_v2.py","lines":["@@ -7,6 +7,12 @@"," General configuration instructions and general remarks are documented"," in the :ref:`execution module docs <x509-setup>`."," ","+.. versionchanged:: 3009.0","+","+    Deprecated arguments and legacy X.509 input formats are no longer","+    accepted. See :ref:`x509-migration-3009` for replacements and changes","+    to the default validity and renewal periods.","+"," .. note::"," ","     Compound matching allowed callers is **not supported** with salt-ssh","@@ -337,20 +343,7 @@ def create_certificate(","             **kwargs,","         )"," ","-    # `algorithm` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium);","-    # use `digest`. `text`, `version`, and `serial_bits` were ignored kwargs","-    # removed in the same release.","-    for removed in (\"algorithm\", \"text\", \"version\", \"serial_bits\"):","-        if removed in kwargs:","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                f\"Keyword argument `{removed}` was removed in 3009.0. \"","-                f\"{'Use `digest` instead.' if removed == 'algorithm' else 'Remove it from the call.'}\"","-            )","-    kwargs = x509util.ensure_cert_kwargs_compat(kwargs)","-","-    if \"days_valid\" not in kwargs and \"not_after\" not in kwargs:","-        # Default changed from 365 to 30 in 3009.0 (Potassium).","-        kwargs[\"days_valid\"] = 30","+    x509util.validate_cert_kwargs(kwargs)"," ","     if encoding not in [\"der\", \"pem\", \"pkcs7_der\", \"pkcs7_pem\", \"pkcs12\"]:","         raise CommandExecutionError(","@@ -522,26 +515,7 @@ def get_signing_policy(signing_policy, ca_server=None):","         # only hand out copies of the cached policy","         policy = copy.deepcopy(__context__[ckey][ca_server][signing_policy])"," ","-    # Long-form name-attribute and extension aliases (e.g. ``commonName``","-    # for ``CN``, ``X509v3 Basic Constraints`` for ``basicConstraints``)","-    # were accepted with a deprecation warning through 3008.x and removed","-    # in 3009.0 (Potassium). Signing policies must use short names.","-    for name, long_names in x509util.NAME_ATTRS_ALT_NAMES.items():","-        for long_name in long_names:","-            if long_name in policy:","-                raise CommandExecutionError(","-                    f\"{signing_policy} contains the long-form name \"","-                    f\"attribute `{long_name}` which was removed in 3009.0.\"","-                    f\" Use the short name `{name}` instead.\"","-                )","-    for extname, long_names in x509util.EXTENSIONS_ALT_NAMES.items():","-        for long_name in long_names:","-            if long_name in policy:","-                raise CommandExecutionError(","-                    f\"{signing_policy} contains the long-form extension \"","-                    f\"`{long_name}` which was removed in 3009.0. Use the \"","-                    f\"short name `{extname}` instead.\"","-                )","+    x509util.validate_cert_kwargs(policy)","     return policy"," "," "],"additions":8,"deletions":34,"truncated":false},{"path":"salt/modules/tls.py","lines":["@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@ def __virtual__():","             False,","             \"pyOpenSSL {} no longer exposes the legacy X509Extension / \"","             \"X509Req / PKCS12 / CRL APIs that salt.modules.tls depends \"","-            \"on. Use salt.modules.x509 (backed by the cryptography \"","+            \"on. Use salt.modules.x509_v2 (backed by the cryptography \"","             \"package) instead.\".format(OpenSSL_version),","         )","     if OpenSSL_version < Version(\"0.14\"):"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"salt/modules/x509_v2.py","lines":["@@ -126,8 +126,15 @@","       with the items taken from the signing policy having priority."," "," ","-Breaking changes versus the previous ``x509`` modules","-~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~","+.. _x509-migration-3009:","+","+Migration from older x509 modules","+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~","+","+The following changes were introduced by the cryptography-based","+``x509_v2`` modules, available since Salt 3006.0 and the default since","+Salt 3008.0:","+"," * The ``public_key`` parameter to ``x509.certificate_managed`` (and corresponding","   ``x509.create_certificate``) used to accept a private key.","   The new modules require an actual public key if this parameter is specified.","@@ -160,19 +167,76 @@","       ca_server:","         - match.compound_matches"," ","-Note that when a ``ca_server`` is involved, both peers must use the updated module version.","+When using remote signing with ``ca_server``, both the requesting minion","+and the CA minion must use the ``x509_v2`` implementation.","+","+The remaining compatibility behavior was removed in Salt 3009:","+","+.. versionchanged:: 3009.0","+","+    Removed compatibility with deprecated arguments, attribute and extension","+    names, and CRL entry formats. The announced validity and renewal defaults","+    now apply unconditionally.","+","+The original M2Crypto-based execution and state modules have been removed.","+The cryptography-based ``x509_v2`` modules are now the only implementation","+of ``x509``. Remove ``features: {x509_v2: false}`` from minion configuration;","+it no longer selects the old implementation.","+","+These changes apply to the ``x509_v2`` execution and state modules, exposed as","+``x509``, and to the Salt SSH wrapper. Update requests, state declarations,","+and signing policies that use the removed forms:","+","+* Use ``digest`` instead of ``algorithm`` when creating certificates or CSRs.","+* Use ``keysize`` instead of ``bits`` when creating or managing private keys.","+* Remove obsolete arguments: ``text``, ``version``, and ``serial_bits`` for","+  certificates; ``text`` and ``version`` for CSRs; ``text`` for CRLs; and","+  ``cipher``, ``verbose``, and ``text`` for private keys. These arguments are","+  rejected instead of being ignored.","+* Remove ``asObj`` from calls to ``x509.get_public_key``. The function returns","+  a PEM-encoded public key.","+* Use canonical attribute names, such as ``CN`` instead of ``commonName`` and","+  ``O`` instead of ``organizationName``. Use canonical extension names, such","+  as ``basicConstraints`` instead of ``X509v3 Basic Constraints`` and","+  ``issuerAltName`` instead of the misspelled ``issuserAltName``. This also","+  applies to attributes and extensions in signing policies.","+* Specify revoked certificates as a simple list of dictionaries, rather than","+  a mapping containing a list of individual fields. Move the legacy","+  ``reason`` field into ``extensions:CRLReason``. For example:","+","+  .. code-block:: yaml","+","+      revoked:","+        - certificate: /etc/pki/certs/revoked.crt","+          extensions:","+            CRLReason: keyCompromise","+","+The default validity and renewal periods have changed:","+","+.. list-table:: Default periods in days","+   :header-rows: 1","+","+   * - Parameter","+     - Before Salt 3009","+     - Salt 3009","+   * - Certificate ``days_valid``","+     - 365","+     - 30","+   * - Certificate state ``days_remaining``","+     - 90","+     - 7","+   * - CRL ``days_valid``","+     - 100","+     - 7","+   * - CRL state ``days_remaining``","+     - 30","+     - 3","+","+Set these parameters explicitly if your deployment requires different","+periods. A certificate's explicit ``not_after`` takes precedence over","+``days_valid``. ``days_remaining`` controls when the corresponding state","+renews an existing certificate or CRL."," ","-Revert to old modules","-~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~","-Until they are removed, you can still revert to the deprecated ``x509`` modules","-by setting the following minion configuration value:","-","-.. code-block:: yaml","-","-    # /etc/salt/minion.d/x509.conf","-","-    features:","-      x509_v2: false"," "," .. _x509-setup:"," \"\"\"","@@ -198,7 +262,6 @@"," "," from collections import OrderedDict"," ","-import salt.utils.dictupdate"," import salt.utils.files"," import salt.utils.functools"," import salt.utils.stringutils","@@ -509,20 +572,7 @@ def create_certificate("," ","         For more information, visit the `OpenSSL docs <https://www.openssl.org/docs/man3.0/man5/x509v3_config.html>`_.","     \"\"\"","-    # `algorithm` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium);","-    # use `digest`. `text`, `version`, and `serial_bits` were ignored kwargs","-    # removed in the same release.","-    for removed in (\"algorithm\", \"text\", \"version\", \"serial_bits\"):","-        if removed in kwargs:","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                f\"Keyword argument `{removed}` was removed in 3009.0. \"","-                f\"{'Use `digest` instead.' if removed == 'algorithm' else 'Remove it from the call.'}\"","-            )","-    kwargs = x509util.ensure_cert_kwargs_compat(kwargs)","-","-    if \"days_valid\" not in kwargs and \"not_after\" not in kwargs:","-        # Default changed from 365 to 30 in 3009.0 (Potassium).","-        kwargs[\"days_valid\"] = 30","+    x509util.validate_cert_kwargs(kwargs)"," ","     if encoding not in [\"der\", \"pem\", \"pkcs7_der\", \"pkcs7_pem\", \"pkcs12\"]:","         raise CommandExecutionError(","@@ -891,7 +941,7 @@ def create_crl("," ","     days_valid","         The number of days the CRL should be valid for. This sets the ``Next Update``","-        field. Defaults to ``100`` (until v3009) or ``7`` (from v3009 onwards).","+        field. Defaults to ``7``."," ","     digest","         The hashing algorithm to use for the signature. Valid values are:","@@ -950,8 +1000,6 @@ def create_crl(","     raw","         Return the encoded raw bytes instead of a string. Defaults to false.","     \"\"\"","-    # `text` was ignored (compat with the pre-x509_v2 module). Removed in","-    # 3009.0 (Potassium); unknown kwargs are rejected.","     if kwargs:","         unknown = [kwarg for kwarg in kwargs if not kwarg.startswith(\"_\")]","         if unknown:","@@ -960,26 +1008,9 @@ def create_crl(","             )"," ","     if days_valid is None:","-        # Default changed from 100 to 7 in 3009.0 (Potassium).","         days_valid = 7"," ","-    # ``revoked`` must be a flat list of dicts and must spell the revocation","-    # reason via ``extensions:CRLReason``. The dict-of-key-to-list wrapper","-    # and the top-level ``reason`` key were accepted (with a deprecation","-    # warning) through 3008.x; both were removed in 3009.0 (Potassium).","-    for rev in revoked:","-        if len(rev) == 1 and isinstance(rev[next(iter(rev))], list):","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                \"Revoked certificates must be specified as a flat list of \"","-                \"dicts. The {<key>: [<dict>, ...]} wrapper is no longer \"","-                \"accepted (removed in 3009.0).\"","-            )","-        if \"reason\" in rev:","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                \"The top-level `reason` key for revoked certificates is no \"","-                \"longer accepted (removed in 3009.0). Specify the reason \"","-                \"via `extensions:CRLReason` instead.\"","-            )","+    x509util.validate_revoked(revoked)"," ","     if encoding not in [\"der\", \"pem\"]:","         raise CommandExecutionError(","@@ -1119,16 +1150,7 @@ def create_csr(","         (``authorityInfoAccess``, ``authorityKeyIdentifier``,","         ``issuerAltName``, ``crlDistributionPoints``).","     \"\"\"","-    # `algorithm` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium);","-    # use `digest`. `text` and `version` were ignored kwargs removed in the","-    # same release.","-    for removed in (\"algorithm\", \"text\", \"version\"):","-        if removed in kwargs:","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                f\"Keyword argument `{removed}` was removed in 3009.0. \"","-                f\"{'Use `digest` instead.' if removed == 'algorithm' else 'Remove it from the call.'}\"","-            )","-    kwargs = x509util.ensure_cert_kwargs_compat(kwargs)","+    x509util.validate_cert_kwargs(kwargs)"," ","     if encoding not in [\"der\", \"pem\"]:","         raise CommandExecutionError(","@@ -1263,9 +1285,6 @@ def create_private_key(","     raw","         Return the encoded raw bytes instead of a string. Defaults to false.","     \"\"\"","-    # `bits` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium); use","-    # `keysize`. `cipher`, `verbose`, and `text` were ignored kwargs removed","-    # in the same release.","     unknown = [kwarg for kwarg in kwargs if not kwarg.startswith(\"_\")]","     if unknown:","         raise SaltInvocationError(f\"Unrecognized keyword arguments: {list(unknown)}\")","@@ -1580,7 +1599,6 @@ def get_public_key(key, passphrase=None):","     passphrase","         If ``key`` is encrypted, the passphrase to decrypt it.","     \"\"\"","-    # `asObj` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium).","     try:","         return x509util.to_pem(x509util.load_pubkey(key)).decode()","     except (CommandExecutionError, SaltInvocationError):","@@ -1657,26 +1675,7 @@ def get_signing_policy(signing_policy, ca_server=None):","         # only hand out copies of the cached policy","         policy = copy.deepcopy(__context__[ckey][ca_server][signing_policy])"," ","-    # Long-form name-attribute and extension aliases (e.g. ``commonName``","-    # for ``CN``, ``X509v3 Basic Constraints`` for ``basicConstraints``)","-    # were accepted with a deprecation warning through 3008.x and removed","-    # in 3009.0 (Potassium). Signing policies must use short names.","-    for name, long_names in x509util.NAME_ATTRS_ALT_NAMES.items():","-        for long_name in long_names:","-            if long_name in policy:","-                raise CommandExecutionError(","-                    f\"{signing_policy} contains the long-form name \"","-                    f\"attribute `{long_name}` which was removed in 3009.0.\"","-                    f\" Use the short name `{name}` instead.\"","-                )","-    for extname, long_names in x509util.EXTENSIONS_ALT_NAMES.items():","-        for long_name in long_names:","-            if long_name in policy:","-                raise CommandExecutionError(","-                    f\"{signing_policy} contains the long-form extension \"","-                    f\"`{long_name}` which was removed in 3009.0. Use the \"","-                    f\"short name `{extname}` instead.\"","-                )","+    x509util.validate_cert_kwargs(policy)","     return policy"," "," "],"additions":83,"deletions":84,"truncated":false},{"path":"salt/states/x509_v2.py","lines":["@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@"," Configuration instructions and general remarks are documented"," in the :ref:`execution module docs <x509-setup>`."," ","+.. versionchanged:: 3009.0","+","+    Deprecated arguments and legacy X.509 input formats are no longer","+    accepted. See :ref:`x509-migration-3009` for replacements and changes","+    to the default validity and renewal periods.","+"," For the list of breaking changes versus the previous ``x509`` modules,"," please also refer to the :ref:`execution module docs <x509-setup>`."," ","@@ -210,8 +216,6 @@"," def __virtual__():","     if not HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY:","         return (False, \"Could not load cryptography\")","-    if not __opts__[\"features\"].get(\"x509_v2\", True):","-        return (False, \"x509_v2 modules were explicitly disabled in `features:x509_v2`\")","     return __virtualname__"," "," ","@@ -257,7 +261,7 @@ def certificate_managed(","     days_remaining","         The certificate will be recreated once the remaining certificate validity","         period is less than this number of days.","-        Defaults to ``90`` (until v3009) or ``7`` (from v3009 onwards).","+        Defaults to ``7``."," ","     ca_server","         Request a remotely signed certificate from ca_server. For this to","@@ -373,7 +377,7 @@ def certificate_managed(","     days_valid","         If ``not_after`` is unspecified, the number of days from the time of issuance","         the certificate should be valid for.","-        Defaults to ``365`` (until v3009) or ``30`` (from v3009 onwards).","+        Defaults to ``30``."," ","     pkcs12_passphrase","         When encoding a certificate as ``pkcs12``, encrypt it with this passphrase.","@@ -396,22 +400,13 @@ def certificate_managed(","         :py:func:`x509.create_certificate <salt.modules.x509_v2.create_certificate>`","         for an overview.","     \"\"\"","-    # `algorithm` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium);","-    # use `digest`.","-    if \"algorithm\" in kwargs:","-        raise SaltInvocationError(","-            \"Keyword argument `algorithm` was removed in 3009.0. \"","-            \"Use `digest` instead.\"","-        )","     if days_valid is None and not_after is None:","-        # Default changed from 365 to 30 in 3009.0 (Potassium).","         days_valid = 30"," ","     if days_remaining is None:","-        # Default changed from 90 to 7 in 3009.0 (Potassium).","         days_remaining = 7"," ","-    kwargs = x509util.ensure_cert_kwargs_compat(kwargs)","+    x509util.validate_cert_kwargs(kwargs)"," ","     ret = {","         \"name\": name,","@@ -662,7 +657,7 @@ def crl_managed(","     days_remaining","         The certificate revocation list will be recreated once the remaining","         CRL validity period is less than this number of days.","-        Defaults to ``30`` (until v3009) or ``3`` (from v3009 onwards).","+        Defaults to ``3``.","         Set to 0 to disable automatic renewal without anything changing."," ","     signing_cert","@@ -676,7 +671,7 @@ def crl_managed("," ","     days_valid","         The number of days that the CRL should be valid for. This sets the ``Next Update``","-        field in the CRL. Defaults to ``100`` (until v3009) or ``7`` (from v3009 onwards).","+        field in the CRL. Defaults to ``7``."," ","     digest","         The hashing algorithm to use for the signature. Valid values are:","@@ -720,38 +715,13 @@ def crl_managed(","             - extensions:","                 cRLNumber: auto","     \"\"\"","-    # `text` was ignored (compat with the pre-x509_v2 module). Removed in","-    # 3009.0 (Potassium).","-    if \"text\" in kwargs:","-        raise SaltInvocationError(","-            \"Keyword argument `text` was removed in 3009.0. Remove it from the call.\"","-        )","-","     if days_valid is None:","-        # Default changed from 100 to 7 in 3009.0 (Potassium).","         days_valid = 7"," ","     if days_remaining is None:","-        # Default changed from 30 to 3 in 3009.0 (Potassium).","         days_remaining = 3"," ","-    # ``revoked`` must be a flat list of dicts and must spell the revocation","-    # reason via ``extensions:CRLReason``. The dict-of-key-to-list wrapper","-    # and the top-level ``reason`` key were accepted (with a deprecation","-    # warning) through 3008.x; both were removed in 3009.0 (Potassium).","-    for rev in revoked:","-        if len(rev) == 1 and isinstance(rev[next(iter(rev))], list):","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                \"Revoked certificates must be specified as a flat list of \"","-                \"dicts. The {<key>: [<dict>, ...]} wrapper is no longer \"","-                \"accepted (removed in 3009.0).\"","-            )","-        if \"reason\" in rev:","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                \"The top-level `reason` key for revoked certificates is no \"","-                \"longer accepted (removed in 3009.0). Specify the reason \"","-                \"via `extensions:CRLReason` instead.\"","-            )","+    x509util.validate_revoked(revoked)"," ","     ret = {","         \"name\": name,","@@ -987,14 +957,7 @@ def csr_managed(","         (``authorityInfoAccess``, ``authorityKeyIdentifier``,","         ``issuerAltName``, ``crlDistributionPoints``).","     \"\"\"","-    # `algorithm` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium);","-    # use `digest`.","-    if \"algorithm\" in kwargs:","-        raise SaltInvocationError(","-            \"Keyword argument `algorithm` was removed in 3009.0. \"","-            \"Use `digest` instead.\"","-        )","-    kwargs = x509util.ensure_cert_kwargs_compat(kwargs)","+    x509util.validate_cert_kwargs(kwargs)"," ","     ret = {","         \"name\": name,","@@ -1251,16 +1214,6 @@ def private_key_managed(","               - x509: /etc/pki/www.crt","         {%- endif %}","     \"\"\"","-    # `bits` was deprecated in 3007.0 and removed in 3009.0 (Potassium); use","-    # `keysize`. `cipher`, `verbose`, and `text` were ignored kwargs removed","-    # in the same release.","-    for removed in (\"bits\", \"cipher\", \"verbose\", \"text\"):","-        if removed in kwargs:","-            raise SaltInvocationError(","-                f\"Keyword argument `{removed}` was removed in 3009.0. \"","-                f\"{'Use `keysize` instead.' if removed == 'bits' else 'Remove it from the call.'}\"","-            )","-","     ret = {","         \"name\": name,","         \"changes\": {},"],"additions":13,"deletions":60,"truncated":false},{"path":"salt/utils/x509.py","lines":["@@ -20,7 +20,6 @@"," import salt.utils.files"," import salt.utils.immutabletypes as immutabletypes"," import salt.utils.stringutils","-import salt.utils.versions"," from salt.exceptions import CommandExecutionError, SaltInvocationError"," "," try:","@@ -284,29 +283,34 @@ def __init__(self):","         super().__init__(\"Private key is unencrypted. Please remove the password.\")"," "," ","-def ensure_cert_kwargs_compat(kwargs):","-    \"\"\"","-    Reject the long form of Name Attribute and extension definitions.","-","-    These were accepted with a deprecation warning through 3008.x and","-    removed in 3009.0 (Potassium). Callers must use the short names.","-    \"\"\"","-    for name, long_names in NAME_ATTRS_ALT_NAMES.items():","-        for long_name in long_names:","-            if long_name in kwargs:","-                raise CommandExecutionError(","-                    f\"Keyword argument `{long_name}` was removed in 3009.0.\"","-                    f\" Use the short name `{name}` instead.\"","+def validate_cert_kwargs(kwargs):","+    \"\"\"Reject legacy X.509 arguments removed in Salt 3009.\"\"\"","+    for name, aliases in {**NAME_ATTRS_ALT_NAMES, **EXTENSIONS_ALT_NAMES}.items():","+        for alias in aliases:","+            if alias in kwargs:","+                raise SaltInvocationError(","+                    f\"`{alias}` is no longer supported. Use `{name}` instead.\"","                 )","+    if \"algorithm\" in kwargs:","+        raise SaltInvocationError(","+            \"`algorithm` is no longer supported. Use `digest` instead.\"","+        )","+    removed = sorted({\"text\", \"version\", \"serial_bits\"}.intersection(kwargs))","+    if removed:","+        raise SaltInvocationError(f\"Unrecognized keyword arguments: {removed}\")"," ","-    for extname, long_names in EXTENSIONS_ALT_NAMES.items():","-        for long_name in long_names:","- 